{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6","id":1156649,"title":"Opinions on Rank 6","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-07T06:05:10-08:00","id":1156649,"title":"Opinions on Rank 6","content":"A topic that has been poorly covered in my opinion is what it means to be and how one gets to rank 6. I'll admit I'm drawn to it because sometimes I want to play big legendary characters. Has anyone put much thought into how players could reach this Rank? Allowed players to reach it? Have you used any as NPCs? I'd be interested to read people's thoughts in the matter as the cannon is peppered with these high level beings, so the writers seemed to like the idea but they never went about giving much time to writing this all up. <br /> <br /> For myself, I was in one campaign where the GM felt that to become a rank 6, it meant you were in a Silver Pack at one point (I know this isn't cannon, but it's how he saw things/wanted to run things). Due to there being a decent write up on Silver Packs, he saw it as a way to model the use of Rank 6s in his game.<br /> <br /> So, anyone else up for sharing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T09:08:15-08:00","id":1156706,"title":"","content":"Not really something I'd ever allow a player to reach. Rank 6 is roughly as a 4th generation metuselah in your Vampire campaign... don't know, Karsh, Baba Yaga, Ur-Shulgi, Kementiri. And it really feels wrong to have a player handle the world that way. At that level of power and renown it's not even the same game, you'd better off playing Exalted.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong in having Albrecht show up at a certain point to reassign a lost Caern and stir some trouble up with people that don't want to lose it, but keep in mind that NPCs should never outshine PCs. Yes, a Rank 6 can maybe reshape a whole country overnight, that's why he's better suited to do that somewhere else, otherwise your game world is just you playing and players watching.<br /> <br /> I don't plan of having my players ever move higher than Rank 4, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T10:38:44-08:00","id":1156730,"title":"","content":"Never played/ran a game that long. The highest I've seen a PC get to is Rank 4. NPCs at Rank 5.<br /> <br /> I would imagine it would take several years to reach that point. I don't know how I feel about it personally. I know their powers are immense and I would cation against it. However if the player earns it, why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T10:46:46-08:00","id":1156731,"title":"","content":"THE GREATEST HONOR: LEGEND<br /> Truly exceptional Garou beyond Rank Five exist.<br /> These legends are given special rewards for their courage<br /> and service to Gaia, and their names are spoken<br /> with the same reverence that we have for Hercules,<br /> Miyamoto Musashi, and Joan of Arc.<br /> However, such advancement is beyond the mere<br /> acquisition of Renown. Legends are part of an exclusive<br /> group, and to qualify, a prospective Elder Garou<br /> must distinguish herself in an extraordinary fashion<br /> more than once. The attainment of the Legend Rank<br /> has nothing whatsoever to do with rules \u2014 it\u2019s purely<br /> a matter of personal judgment on your part, and if<br /> there\u2019s any doubt in your mind whether or not she<br /> has surpassed the mighty deeds of even the greatest<br /> of Elders, she hasn\u2019t. Only when there\u2019s absolutely no<br /> question of the character\u2019s legendary status should you<br /> consider letting her strive for this Rank.<br /> When an Elder\u2019s reputation spreads so far throughout<br /> the Garou Nation that it reaches the ears of existing<br /> Legends, one member takes it upon himself to travel<br /> to the caern of the Elder in question and investigate<br /> her worthiness. Once he has satisfied himself as to the<br /> candidate\u2019s worthiness (or unworthiness), he contacts<br /> three other Legends to present his case. If he convinced<br /> them that the candidate is truly worthy, all four Legends<br /> arrive at the caern of the candidate and challenge the<br /> subject. If the candidate succeeds, she undergoes a special<br /> version of the Rite of Accomplishment performed in<br /> tandem by the Legends along with the Master of the<br /> Rite of the candidate\u2019s caern (as a courtesy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:15:41-08:00","id":1156739,"title":"","content":"I feel that Legendary characters should be the equivalent of the mythic heroes of our legends - Hercules, Jason, Achilles, and Odysseus. Legendary Garou should be those who made the first Pact with spirits, created the common rites still used today, secured the Incarna patronage of the tribes, slayed the Zmei, and did the other great acts which all Garou still remember today and tell their stories about. They might include the great war leader of the Get of Fenris who lead his tribe in the invasion of the British Isles and taking of the Fianna caerns there, or the first king of House Wyrmfoe when he established his family as its own dynasty and royal house.<br /> <br /> So I don't feel that there are many Legendary characters in the past few centuries, maybe not even a single one around today. I don't agree that there are several at any one point in time who are there to evaluate and confirm another entry into Legendary status (I understand Moirdryd is quoting from the W20 books, I just disagree with the book). These are the kind of people that don't even come once in a generation or even once in a lifetime. They are very rare now - the world is not like it was in the Early Times when the great heroes of the Garou accomplished great things. There might be one Legendary every few centuries although there might be certain important events where Garou rose to the occassion and several Legends were established at the same time, or near the same time period.<br /> <br /> To me, a Garou reaches Legendary status when the rest of the Nation treats him as such. That means his exploits are so well known and so grand, that other Garou around the world - regardless of tribe - start telling each other stories of that Garou's exploits. Athros and even other Elders constantly challenge him in order to prove their worth, but they fail - and eventually people stop trying because it is obvious what kind of Garou he is.<br /> <br /> So a PC has to have the exploits needed in order to accomplish this (which will take a long time as he does quests as an Elder), and then defeat a variety of challengers to assert his supremacy in his auspice field. At that point, once the ST believes he's done that, the character might receive some kind of vision from Gaia, tribal totem, or something else (this might also occur to some other Garou who is then quested to tell the prospective Legend what to do and be his witness) that effectively gives him the quest that once accomplished, confirms his Legendary status. At that point, he might begin asking to be taught the Rank 6 Gifts.<br /> <br /> The ST should have high standards and expectations for any PC to do this. But I think it is up to the PC to try and convince the ST that his character is accomplishing this. I think the PC should take the lead, with the ST collaborating with him and being very clear which of his ideas work or don't contribute to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:49:35-08:00","id":1156747,"title":"","content":"To be fair as the Apocalypse war grows the ability to become Legend grows likewise. There are fewer Legends in the world born out of peace than conflict for example. I see no issue with there being the Rank 6 characters as have been presented to us in the stories and background material for Werewolf. After all there are only a half dozen or so currently in the Nation and most of them didn't go through the Rite as described above but were basically recognized as such by the Celestines and so forth, the likes of Golgol Fangs First, The Margrave and Albrecht certainly being worthy of the acclamation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T14:07:20-08:00","id":1156790,"title":"","content":"I actually have a rank 6 player and I can easily say that he is the only That ever deserved that status from feats no other character ever managed to achieve. He was mostly local hero of elder status but still he was highly active in fighting the wyrm and organizing his sept. That of course is not enough. The real thing came when elders from other countries that visited the sept heard imposible feats of heroism from that elder monster, like killing ancient wyrm horrors single handendly while warbands of garou failed to. The first active Rank 6 who took note of this heroe's achievements was Grimfang rebirthed and masqueraded as a freshly changed cub, spreading the word that was the seed of a new Legend.<br /> I even made 2 new rank 6 gifts for him.<br /> <br /> So yes, a rank 6 character passes to the domain of legends, epic stats, maybe above 5, epic unique or rare high point merits, and some Gifts with unique never seen before powers.<br /> Truth said many rank 6 gifts are weak for the rank they are supposed to be owned, but well you can always modify them to your liking.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T14:11:56-08:00","id":1156793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156790#post1156790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have a rank 6 player and I can easily say that he is the only That ever deserved that status from feats no other character ever managed to achieve. He was mostly local hero of elder status but still he was highly active in fighting the wyrm and organizing his sept. That of course is not enough. The real thing came when elders from other countries that visited the sept heard imposible feats of heroism from that elder monster, like killing ancient wyrm horrors single handendly while warbands of garou failed to. The first active Rank 6 who took note of this heroe's achievements was Grimfang rebirthed and masqueraded as a freshly changed cub, spreading the word that was the seed of a new Legend.<br /> I even made 2 new rank 6 gifts for him.<br /> <br /> So yes, a rank 6 character passes to the domain of legends, epic stats, maybe above 5, epic unique or rare high point merits, and some Gifts with unique never seen before powers.<br /> Truth said many rank 6 gifts are weak for the rank they are supposed to be owned, but well you can always modify them to your liking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be curious to see what your write up was. I know the idea is unpopular for some, but its something I've always been curious about. For how people talk about the rank, and what it takes to earn it, I feel like there are a lot of Rank 6 characters in cannon (Black Tooth, Albrecht, Margrave, Grim Fang, Golgol, Cries in the Wind...am I missing any?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T16:46:34-08:00","id":1156836,"title":"","content":"I like to try several play styles, so though most of the time I prefer to stick to low-ranking Garou, and even cubs, I had also my share of elder's games, and on some of them I got PCs on Rank 6.<br /> <br /> The first thing, already pointed out, is that most Rank 6 Gifts are terribly written. Albrecht's Renew the Cycle is unusable in RAW, just to name one.<br /> <br /> But lets see... the cannon answer was presented, but as most I feel it ludicrous. Not only it makes it seems that a number of Legends at a time is not only common, but even expected. It makes it seems that the Legendary heroes form a kind of closed club that set aside all their differences to get along and talk about how they are bad-asses. The cannon Legends are many, and though I can see the point on most of them, it is kind of lame to make so much as, well, cannon.<br /> <br /> For a PC to get to Legend, I would either require a helluva lot of accomplishments... or just assume this is the intended power level of the story at some point. I strongly endorse the later. You never should let a player get to Legend without intending it for your game. And be sure that the players are either to be all Legends, or be in agreement with the result. A good start for making it during the game would be for the group as a whole act as jury over the matter, and the rank-up occurring only at an unanimous agreement. If you can't convince a fellow player that you do deserve it, then you probably don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T18:20:56-08:00","id":1156853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156790#post1156790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes, a rank 6 character passes to the domain of legends, epic stats, maybe above 5, epic unique or rare high point merits, and some Gifts with unique never seen before powers.<br /> Truth said many rank 6 gifts are weak for the rank they are supposed to be owned, but well you can always modify them to your liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes quite obvious that you're running a powerplay campaign. By all means have fun, but it's really not a style I can endorse and as far as I'm concerned it's not even roleplay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156739#post1156739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't feel that there are many Legendary characters in the past few centuries, maybe not even a single one around today.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much share your vision.<br /> I think that canon-wise Albrecht is supposed to be Rank 6 after his retrieval of the Silver Crown, just like Margrave Konietzko and Zhyzhak. I'm unaware of other Legends of the Garou around the world but they're probably less than a dozen in total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T18:28:01-08:00","id":1156856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156853#post1156853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes quite obvious that you're running a powerplay campaign. By all means have fun, but it's really not a style I can endorse and as far as I'm concerned it's not even roleplay.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this style of response really needed though? You can disagree and prefer lower powered games, but honestly I don't see how that makes your style better then others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T18:57:54-08:00","id":1156863,"title":"","content":"Rank 6 is something you're not going to see in most games. IIRC until Revised the only character to have a Rank 6 listing was Golgol Fangs First. They are the rarest of the rare and you only get there through acknowledgment of other living Legends of the Garou or through equal similar proclamations.<br /> <br /> Given that the most important characters in a chronicle are your players characters it's entirely possible that they may well strive to become Legends and one or two might even make it. Of course Rank 5 is the target most people go for and many may not ever make it past Adren but it's like higher rank gifts and Grand Klaives and so forth, you can restrict as you see fit but ultimately they were put in there for a PC to use. I am in the process in fact of setting up a new chronicle and my p[layers asked &quot;What Tribe, Fetish, Camp restrictions&quot; to my response of &quot;This time folks, as long as it's from the Chargen chapter of W20, create as you want&quot;. I;ve a mix of very old hands and one or two shiny newbies to Werewolf and they're all excited on having some free reign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T19:06:02-08:00","id":1156865,"title":"","content":"Well 1st ed also had Grimfang a Silver Fang and Cries in the Wind for Rank 6. So 1st ed had 3 already listed specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T19:08:37-08:00","id":1156866,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=<br /> <br /> Given that the most important characters in a chronicle are your players characters it's entirely possible that they may well strive to become Legends and one or two might even make it. Of course Rank 5 is the target most people go for and many may not ever make it past Adren but it's like higher rank gifts and Grand Klaives and so forth, you can restrict as you see fit but ultimately they were put in there for a PC to use. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> This is my thoughts right here. This is stuff provided by the writers of the setting. Someone using these power levels isn't necessarily wrong. You may not prefer it which is fine, you may not allow it in your games, again fine. I just think its wrong to say that those who use it are &quot;not role playing&quot; or not playing Werewolf the Apocalypse correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-07-2017, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T19:30:54-08:00","id":1156871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156856#post1156856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this style of response really needed though? You can disagree and prefer lower powered games, but honestly I don't see how that makes your style better then others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason to hide my thoughts on role playing on a role playing forum. It's not like I insulted anyone.<br /> As far as entertainment goes there is no &quot;right&quot; thing to like; still, we have shows for kids and shows for adults, well-written plots and lousy scripts. Saying that rank 6 gifts are underpowered means running a show for kids, and adding that a player became rank 6 in that context probably also means lousy script (I might be wrong, of course).<br /> But people can still enjoy a Bleach tankobon even if no one in his sane mind would ever compare it to Shakespeare, so why is there an issue if I mislike it?<br /> <br /> Also, my style is better because it's mine. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-07-2017, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T19:37:30-08:00","id":1156874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156853#post1156853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes quite obvious that you're running a powerplay campaign. By all means have fun, but it's really not a style I can endorse and as far as I'm concerned it's not even roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flashback post to the 90s!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T20:09:30-08:00","id":1156882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156871#post1156871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see no reason to hide my thoughts on role playing on a role playing forum. It's not like I insulted anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You called it lousy, for children, and not even a role play. That is insulting someone. You can disagree with the op and still be respectful about it. <br /> <br /> As for getting to rank 6, I'd have to be really wowed. I don't know what that would entail though. I've never seen a player character do anything worth reaching rank 6 in my opinion. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15478-celinikal","name":"celinikal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T03:50:34-08:00","id":1156954,"title":"","content":"We had a chronicle where it happened, to one of the three Player Characters. It was awesome. We started out as a random Pack of a Wendigo (Rides-the-Wind), a Glasswalker (Joseph Watson, later known as Angel of the Web, my character) and a Fianna (Skyhowl). We did some crazy stuff, it was a true roller coaster. We saw a Caern die, fought Wyrm Monsters, cleansed an ancient Mokole, killed a bunch of Ratkin, befriended a Gurhal, ripped open a hive and cleansed the Totem within it. Made friends, watched friends die. Found one of Rorgs missing teeth and sought the personal wisdom of Helios. We defended the Garden of Eshtarra and dragged an Elder of the Society of Nidhogg into Erebus. That and a few things more got us to Rank 4. <br /> <br /> Then the ST for the chronicle opened up the Croatan Song book (which is where some of Rides character concepts came from initially) and we went and did more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T04:30:58-08:00","id":1156961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156793#post1156793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to see what your write up was. I know the idea is unpopular for some, but its something I've always been curious about. For how people talk about the rank, and what it takes to earn it, I feel like there are a lot of Rank 6 characters in cannon (Black Tooth, Albrecht, Margrave, Grim Fang, Golgol, Cries in the Wind...am I missing any?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup you missed Zhyzhack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, which does not have a rank 6 gift, Cries in the Wind has no Rank 6 gift too.<br /> <br /> Ok here is the exmple of Rank 6 boons of my player's character.<br /> I don't include lower rank gifts and rites and skills coz are pretty much the same for long campaign Elder status characters.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Backgrounds</b></u><br /> Numen (Wendigo) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits</b></u><br /> Immune to Wyrm Emanations (6 points)<br /> Heart of Steel (3 point, Manowar reference): As Iron Will but works on emotional attacks rather than mental ones.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rank 6 Ahroun Gift</b></u><br /> <b>Wrath of the Leaving Breath: </b>The gift enhances the Rage roll to remain active. The werewolf rolls Rage difficulty 8, if he succeeds he heals all health level and the wounds leave no battle scars.<br /> Also the werewolf enters frenzy and all his physical actions have their full dice pools as automatic successes, yes attack ratings still add to the damage total if the gift user hits an enemy.<br /> The werewolf while in this frenzy may spend a willpower and roll an attack but only to check for 10's, with 1's and ignored.<br /> The Gift may be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> Note: This gift exists because its owner achieved the feat of the gift's activation, without actually having this specific gift, yes he got 10 successes of diff 8 in rage roll and<br /> 47 successes on damage one hit KO an impossible enemy. It's a mixture of house joke and traumatic in-game experience.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rank 6 Wendigo Gift</b></u><br /> <b>True Wendigo: </b>The werewolf enters frenzy and transforms to a huge crinos with razor sharp ice dagger fangs and claws, a frozen breath and dead cold eyes, his frame becomes taller and more lean possessed by an eternal hunger (obvious rib bones under lean fur etc etc), his stats become Strength = Rage + 4, dexterity = willpower + 1, Stamina = Willpower +3. All in close combat with the Wendigo automatically lose 2 from all dicepools and gain +1 difficulty to all rolls. All the wendigo's movement count's as dodge on all attacks without penalty, except when he is in grapple, claws and fangs do +3 damage and cause frost bites, further -2 penalty on all rolls and may not be regenerated by normal means. Gifts like mother' touch may be used only if the victim is away from the Wendigo's frost effect (Aka cold breath). In wendigo form the werewolf gains no penalty on attack directed to enemy's heart and will most likely devour it.<br /> Devouring a heart will heal a health level of damage, even aggravated and one willpower Rage or Gnosis.If the Werewolf fails to devourat least one heart Rolls Rage difficulty 4, each success deals one health level of aggravated damage per succes which may not be soaked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-08-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T04:50:08-08:00","id":1156966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156853#post1156853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes quite obvious that you're running a powerplay campaign. By all means have fun, but it's really not a style I can endorse and as far as I'm concerned it's not even roleplay.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>No the campaign is no powerplay at all, yeah the characters are elders and can ruin planets, but shattered planets may devour you inside their explosions. Believe me, they are with the shit in the pants. And the campaign has a completely different kind of roleplay, a campaign is not only about fight , but when fights do happen they are unlikely to what players experienced so far, not from the side of power but from the side of the unknown and the otherworldly. At these levels there is no distinction in auspicies, a werewolf no matter the auspice may be called to take any role at a moment's notice.<br /> In one of the latest encounters the philodox played the role of the ahroun and the ahroun the role of the spirit chaneller. The ahroun's player was facepalming himself screaming &quot;I can't believe it, I became a priest'', *sigh* awesome campaign moments.<br /> <br /> Well in general an elder Rank campaign is a wonderful experience, but it needs preparation, you must have players that reached that status in sacrifice of blood and spirit, you can't just make one evening's elder characters and expect smooth results. Background and real character experience are the keys, and of course love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-08-2017, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T18:43:42-08:00","id":1157167,"title":"","content":"I can't remember where I saw it, so I won't guarantee, but I remember quite a number of official rank 6 Garou, at least a dozen. Just the Silverfangs had three or four.<br /> <br /> About why saying that Rank 6 Gifts are weak...<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Warrior let you make a roll at dif 8 just to get the right to spend Rage on regeneration of non-silver Agg. Since it is without spending your action, it certainly is good, but maybe Rank 3 or 4?<br /> <br /> One on One lets you spend a permanent dot of Gnosis to choose a foe and fight it. Then it lets you all alone where the foe were. It is quite powerful, but given the stingy restrictions, nothing beyond Rank 5.<br /> <br /> Sleep of the Hero lets you spend 2 Gnosis and make a roll at dif 9 to do nothing. Well, technically you resurrects your target, but it will sleep soundly until the Apocalypse, so you really do nothing.<br /> <br /> Then you get Storyteller. You spend 1 perma Gnosis and say shit. Shit is true. Who thought this had any semblance of balance?<br /> <br /> Call Great Fenris isn't bad, just clich\u00e9. I'm pretty sure I saw at least 2 or 3 other Get gifts that call Fenris and he eats your hand. At Rank 6 even calling Great Fenris shouldn't cost your hand. It could cost any number of perma Gnosis or Perma Rage, because you buy them back, but your hand?<br /> <br /> Release from Bondage makes you immune to mystical coercion and able to break it on others by touch, and that is one of the few RAW Gifts I think that qualify for Rank 6. This thing not only can be actually used, it is effectively good.<br /> <br /> Firebringer is an obvious but cool concept. But the efforts to balance it went too far. Every time you're affected by a supernatural power of any kind you can choose to: A) make a journey into the Umbra, then B) work with a spirit C) for a non-disclosed time to D) develop a new Gift <u>based</u> on it E) that you <b><u>can't use</u></b>. You only get to F) spend your time teaching it to others and G) being forever vulnerable to the same power again. Yes, you don't even get to resist it better, you get to resist it worse. It achieves to be worse than Sleep of the Hero.<br /> <br /> Home in All Lands is the second in the list that is actually good. When you step sideways, you can instead teleport, with few restrictions, fair precision and no drawback.<br /> <br /> Shield of Gaia is too open for interpretation to be sure. You choose a modern technology, you become forever immune to it. Simple, can be weak or OP depending on the choice, but mostly ok.<br /> <br /> Renew the Cycle, the famous gift of Lord Albrecht, is worse than useless. You have to win a contested roll between Gnosis and Willpower, can only affect undead, and this thing costs you three perma Gnosis. 3 perma Gnosis to kill a vampire, and you still need to win a contest that isn't rigged in your favor, but against you. Any valid target you have an actual chance of affecting you can also kill with far less effort.<br /> <br /> Thought-Form of the Twelve Ministers is another ok Gift, though nothing so awe-inspiring. 1 temp of each Rage, Gnosis and Will is a little stingy, but can still be used repeatedly, and that is the strong point. You get a set of lousy skill bonuses (+2 Brawl is the biggest concern here), self-cleanse from wyrm-taint (cool and of significance), and the true power, you refreshes Gnosis for every Garou at 10 feet. This last benefit is worth the Rank 6.<br /> <br /> Invoked Presence is interesting, but have much of the same problems of Shield of Gaia. You call the <i>Totem Gift</i> for several hours in a 180 yards radius. Ok, but hard to adapt.<br /> <br /> As In the Beginning is weird. You spend some Gnosis, make a roll, and rips a hole in the Gauntlet. It seems dire, indeed. But the only permanent effect is a reduction of 1 in the Gauntlet that can't be stacked by new uses. Everything else is left so vague that you can't even know how large the affected area is.<br /> <br /> Rebirthing, unique to Grimfang, makes him reincarnate once. It isn't bad, but it is kinda lame.<br /> <br /> Becoming Uktena is finally the worse Rank 6 Gift ever. It is like Call Great Fenris, except that the Uktena called isn't bound to do shit after a turn and you die for good. At least there is no roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T19:00:36-08:00","id":1157172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157167#post1157167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember where I saw it, so I won't guarantee, but I remember quite a number of official rank 6 Garou, at least a dozen. Just the Silverfangs had three or four.<br /> <br /> About why saying that Rank 6 Gifts are weak...<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Warrior let you make a roll at dif 8 just to get the right to spend Rage on regeneration of non-silver Agg. Since it is without spending your action, it certainly is good, but maybe Rank 3 or 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: W20 changed it to simply regenerating aggravated non-silver damage as if it were lethal. This still seems a bit underpowered to me, though. It seems like that should be something that Combat Healing should be doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shield of Gaia is too open for interpretation to be sure. You choose a modern technology, you become forever immune to it. Simple, can be weak or OP depending on the choice, but mostly ok. </div> </div> </div>Rokea also learn it one rank earlier, so it is, technically, not a strict Rank 6 Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Renew the Cycle, the famous gift of Lord Albrecht, is worse than useless. You have to win a contested roll between Gnosis and Willpower, can only affect undead, and this thing costs you three perma Gnosis. 3 perma Gnosis to kill a vampire, and you still need to win a contest that isn't rigged in your favor, but against you. Any valid target you have an actual chance of affecting you can also kill with far less effort. </div> </div> </div>W20 also changed it, though it only grants a greater benefit if the vampire was young or you somehow have way more Gnosis on you than just the typical ten points; else, you'll have to spend more permanent dots to put down a really old one. Young ones, meanwhile, only require one temporary Gnosis or so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Becoming Uktena is finally the worse Rank 6 Gift ever. It is like Call Great Fenris, except that the Uktena called isn't bound to do shit after a turn and you die for good. At least there is no roll. </div> </div> </div>Also, the mechanical benefits are not particularly impressive, particularly in comparison with Fenris's War Avatar, which has Rage and Willpower ratings far exceeding typical spirits ceilings for those traits.<br /> <br /> You left out Dance of Shiva for the Nagah, incidentally. If you crunch the numbers on that, then a specialized character with Dexterity and Performance (dance) both at 5 can potentially incinerate the entire world for 26 dice of aggravated damage (statistically, around 13 levels) after building up from lesser damage and smaller radii of effect (base is four dice to a few yards). It also costs nothing to use. On the flip side, getting such a result requires all ten of your dice getting a result of 10, which is a one in ten billion shot, but the lower levels of effect from less than the total number of successes and nil cost can be potentially effective under other circumstances. As a downside, actually pulling off those more impressive effects goes against the Nagah's surgical mission statement, and is likely to result in one of three strikes applied to you, at the very least. It could be ignored under a total incineration event, I suppose, but only because you incinerated everything for 20+ dice of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T03:31:28-08:00","id":1157238,"title":"","content":"In a general way of thinking, when you are about to create or recreate a rank 6 gift, you must have in mind that it is a gifted power directly from a high umbral god, be it Gaea, Arees, Eelios or whoever, it is an element of above epic proportions, so you must think how this power works when a god is using it. A warrior or beast god with a gift that resembles &quot;Unstoppable Warrior'' for example will not heal one aggravated damage per turn, man even great beasts of pagaea heal two aggravated damage per turn without pausing, so a related god will mostly like heal all damage and keep fighting without wound penalties. So don't feel ashamed if a rank 6 power seems too powerful as long as there is only one character that knows it. Also just because they are powers above elder status being taught by higher beings may not be canceled by lesser, even rank 5 powers. Thats of course a personal taking on the rank 6 issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T07:01:58-08:00","id":1157266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157167#post1157167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About why saying that Rank 6 Gifts are weak...</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, you're using 2nd edition gifts and some have been changed, or just never reprinted.<br /> <br /> Unstoppable warrior, as said, lets you regenerate everything except silver damage, passive. It<br /> <br /> One on One has not been rewritten yet, but the teleportation it's powerful AF, way more than Rank 5 Strider gifts..<br /> <br /> Sleep of the Hero is cool like hell. Ok, you won't do much for your current storyline but you're paving the way for the Apocalypse, it's exactly the kind of feat I'm expecting from a Legend. It's distressing how fast you dismissed this gift, you could run a whole campaign on resurrecting heroes of the modern age.<br /> <br /> Firebringer has been reworked too, you have no Umbral quest or anything. You just need to survive the power (any power) and forever forfeit any kind of defense against it, and the gift is done. You're not allowed to use it, but now there's a type of Gaian spirits that can teach it to the other Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Becoming Uktena is finally the worse Rank 6 Gift ever. It is like Call Great Fenris, except that the Uktena called isn't bound to do shit after a turn and you die for good. At least there is no roll. </div> </div> </div>I'm under the impression that for some reason you think that Rank 6 powers are bound to break the world like imba level 9 Vampire shit. Use your power, win the day, go home. But that's not the feeling the authors wanted to put in Werewolf nor the kind of power Rank 6 are supposed to be. You called <i>lame</i> a power that resurrects you, only because it works once, and <i>bad </i>the war-avatar of Fenris because it costs an hand (and can therefore only be summoned twice). WtA is a story about sacrifice and heroic deeds and it's quite different from a story about heroic powers that makes you win the day by farting fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T08:59:56-08:00","id":1157291,"title":"","content":"I love Becoming Uktena. You don't die, you become a/the Horned Serpent. If I had Becoming Uktena as a character I would have a hard time *not* pulling trigger. I can't think of a happier ending for a Garou's saga.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as I recall, the Uktena of 'Becoming Uktena' didn't have stats. There were some larp rules, I guess, but I am not converting those. I don't think the Utkena in this case is meant to have stats at all; the limit to what you can accomplish is established by your nature and the brevity of your time in the physical world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-09-2017, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T11:54:53-08:00","id":1157328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157238#post1157238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a general way of thinking, when you are about to create or recreate a rank 6 gift, you must have in mind that it is a gifted power directly from a high umbral god, be it Gaea, Arees, Eelios or whoever, it is an element of above epic proportions, so you must think how this power works when a god is using it. A warrior or beast god with a gift that resembles &quot;Unstoppable Warrior'' for example will not heal one aggravated damage per turn, man even great beasts of pagaea heal two aggravated damage per turn without pausing, so a related god will mostly like heal all damage and keep fighting without wound penalties. So don't feel ashamed if a rank 6 power seems too powerful as long as there is only one character that knows it. Also just because they are powers above elder status being taught by higher beings may not be canceled by lesser, even rank 5 powers. Thats of course a personal taking on the rank 6 issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits don't actually have the mechanical use of Gifts they teach in the overwhelming majority of cases. They offer something to a changer, and it produces a new power in the one to whom the Gift is given, irrespective of the capabilities of the giver. Especially notable since the Celestines that teach these Gifts don't have mechanically-defined statistics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, you're using 2nd edition gifts and some have been changed, or just never reprinted.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unstoppable warrior, as said, lets you regenerate everything except silver damage, passive. It</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...is also kind of weak, honestly. Even as a passive, it isn't really quite on par with Break the Bonds or Dance of Shiva.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sleep of the Hero is cool like hell. Ok, you won't do much for your current storyline but you're paving the way for the Apocalypse, it's exactly the kind of feat I'm expecting from a Legend. It's distressing how fast you dismissed this gift, you could run a whole campaign on resurrecting heroes of the modern age.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> It's an odd thing to have as one tribe's Gift, honestly. Membership in the Returning Kings club seems like it might be better as a built-in part of reaching Rank 6.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Firebringer has been reworked too, you have no Umbral quest or anything. You just need to survive the power (any power) and forever forfeit any kind of defense against it, and the gift is done. You're not allowed to use it, but now there's a type of Gaian spirits that can teach it to the other Garou.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The more I think about Firebringer, the more I wonder if pursuit of spiritual knowledge in general might be able to equal or exceed it. After all, there's a vast theoretical trove of untapped Gifts in old legends, Firebringer not required.<br /> <br /> [qote]<br /> I'm under the impression that for some reason you think that Rank 6 powers are bound to break the world like imba level 9 Vampire shit. Use your power, win the day, go home. But that's not the feeling the authors wanted to put in Werewolf nor the kind of power Rank 6 are supposed to be. You called </span></span></span><i>lame</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> a power that resurrects you, only because it works once, and </span></span></span><i>bad </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the war-avatar of Fenris because it costs an hand (and can therefore only be summoned twice). WtA is a story about sacrifice and heroic deeds and it's quite different from a story about heroic powers that makes you win the day by farting fire. [/quote]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Well, Dance of Shiva certainly is capable of breaking the world... it probably won't let you win, so much as flip the table that the board is on, though. And, again, Shield of Gaia is apparently more of an elder thing, since Darkwater Rokea learn C'et's Shell at Rank Five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T13:49:39-08:00","id":1157347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157328#post1157328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirits don't actually have the mechanical use of Gifts they teach in the overwhelming majority of cases. They offer something to a changer, and it produces a new power in the one to whom the Gift is given, irrespective of the capabilities of the giver. Especially notable since the Celestines that teach these Gifts don't have mechanically-defined statistics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The case of a rank 6 gift learning should always be an exception to all that a character has experienced so far.<br /> Actual manifested deities, not through avatars, can actually break the boundaries of reality (and rules) and pass some of their mojo to their chosen champion. Yes the power they may give might not be the perfect sample of their true divine potential, noone would like to see a werewolf that melts the earth where he treads or shatter planets with his blows, but should always be awesomely exceptional, like Hercules who had the strength of his father, but couldn't fly around the earth or throw thunderbolts. And yes the celestines may not have mechanical stats, but they can still be highly conceptual if not specific.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157328#post1157328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm under the impression that for some reason you think that Rank 6 powers are bound to break the world like imba level 9 Vampire shit. Use your power, win the day, go home. But that's not the feeling the authors wanted to put in Werewolf nor the kind of power Rank 6 are supposed to be. You called [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<i>lame</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> a power that resurrects you, only because it works once, and </span></span></span><i>bad </i>[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]the war-avatar of Fenris because it costs an hand (and can therefore only be summoned twice).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even level 9 Disciplines are not world breaking, they are a completely different level of gaming but world breaking, mmm no. Though I am against anything that makes a vamp look like a superhero.<br /> <br /> As for rank 6 Gifts, well they are not disciplines, they are mostly rumored to be history changing elements that when they come to the front they shake the flow of a story, though most representatives may not look like that, STs should be encouraged to make unique gifts or alter mechanics in order to raise both the power in question and the hero that use it to the status they deserve in a given story.<br /> <br /> A warrior that heals instantly all damage he receives, a mystic that is impossible to hurt because of an invincible aura of bliss he exudes, a story teller who alters reality with his fairy tales, a pilgrim who may travel everywhere in the world with one step, a wolf that may not be touched by anything crafted etc etc etc.<br /> Legend, pure legend and atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T14:19:47-08:00","id":1157357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157266#post1157266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you're using 2nd edition gifts and some have been changed, or just never reprinted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, I didn't cared to look further and, in doing so, take a risk. My intent were just in presenting examples, and if they were many, is because I got carried away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157266#post1157266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One on One has not been rewritten yet, but the teleportation it's powerful AF, way more than Rank 5 Strider gifts..</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly it is, and extremely cool. Still, not Rank 6 material on my opinion, since it counterbalances the teleportation effect with heavy restrictions, and the Talon's gift is simpler and more effective on this by far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157266#post1157266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleep of the Hero is cool like hell. Ok, you won't do much for your current storyline but you're paving the way for the Apocalypse, it's exactly the kind of feat I'm expecting from a Legend. It's distressing how fast you dismissed this gift, you could run a whole campaign on resurrecting heroes of the modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it wasn't cool, I said it did nothing <u>as a Rank 6 Gift</u>. For me, it would work far better as a Rank 5 Ritual. Seriously, getting a rare Legend to wander through caerns just to bless the recently dead is kinda weird, to say the least. But a ritual that can be performed by the elders between the People, with such a cost that only great warriors warrant this price, that would be very interesting. A Rank 6 Gift to <u>awaken</u> such heroes would be far more interesting as a Rank 6 Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157266#post1157266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firebringer has been reworked too, you have no Umbral quest or anything. You just need to survive the power (any power) and forever forfeit any kind of defense against it, and the gift is done. You're not allowed to use it, but now there's a type of Gaian spirits that can teach it to the other Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it would work fantastically as a level 5 ritual. I'm not dismissing how cool it is, I actually had a chronicle entirely set around a PC enacting this Gift (it was a solo), and it is very interesting. But as a Rank 6 Gift it is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157266#post1157266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm under the impression that for some reason you think that Rank 6 powers are bound to break the world like imba level 9 Vampire shit. Use your power, win the day, go home. But that's not the feeling the authors wanted to put in Werewolf nor the kind of power Rank 6 are supposed to be. You called <i>lame</i> a power that resurrects you, only because it works once, and <i>bad </i>the war-avatar of Fenris because it costs an hand (and can therefore only be summoned twice). WtA is a story about sacrifice and heroic deeds and it's quite different from a story about heroic powers that makes you win the day by farting fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Keep your lecture on the game to yourself, first and foremost. I got tired of it still in the 90's. I already know what the authors intended, what the game is supposed to do, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> But the question is those powers under the condition of being a Rank 6 Gift. Most of them are really cool ideas that could be explored in other ways. A Rank 6 Gift isn't simply a power. It is a power that:<br /> <br /> 1- Distinguishes a Legend from their lesser peers. It have to be more than a little interesting. It have to speak that the Garou in question is legendary in status. Otherwise, it could be better served as a lesser power;<br /> <br /> 2- Is unreachable by those lesser Garou. Anything that should be doable by lesser werewolves, even if in a weaker way, shouldn't be a Rank 6 Gift;<br /> <br /> 3- Truly unique. If you can picture any reason for it to be done by more than one person, or at any frequency at all, it probably isn't Rank 6 material, either;<br /> <br /> 4- Costs XP and works as a power option. The rules are meant for PCs, so you like it or not, Gifts should be balanced with PCs in mind. If you never want to ST such a level of power, its ok, but the game still should address people who want. The player will pay XP and otherwise work to get this as a power option for the character. Making it a Rank 6 means making it extremely costly. If you make it too weak for its cost, or too hard to use, you have good chances of the player feeling cheated. Even if the player for any reason don't spend the XP, it is still a let down;<br /> <br /> 5- Should be intended for use. It doesn't make sense to create a thing for the game that won't ever see the light of the game. Be it as a weapon in the hands of the PCs, a plot device, or just color background for your chronicle, it should be made in a way that makes sense for it to see play sometimes.<br /> <br /> For example, I reworked Renew the Cycle in my chronicles for it to remove almost any ailment on the target, resetting soundness of body and mind to the target's youth. It still costs 3 Perma Gnosis. I never gave it to any players. It was the sole province of King Albrecht. Some memorable moments of those chronicles came when the PCs witnessed or went through this Gift, generally as the climax of their rewards. In a Mage game, the PCs who went through it were Kinfolk reprogrammed by the Technocracy, and Albrecht cleansed them from the Mind effects of the NOM for the next and final arc of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> The avatar of Fenris have more than one problem, and that is something I already stated. The Get is simply the ribe with more gifts to somehow call their totem, so for more that calling down the Great Fenris can seem cool, it isn't something new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157291#post1157291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Becoming Uktena. You don't die, you become a/the Horned Serpent. If I had Becoming Uktena as a character I would have a hard time *not* pulling trigger. I can't think of a happier ending for a Garou's saga.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as I recall, the Uktena of 'Becoming Uktena' didn't have stats. There were some larp rules, I guess, but I am not converting those. I don't think the Utkena in this case is meant to have stats at all; the limit to what you can accomplish is established by your nature and the brevity of your time in the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is certainly a fine ending for someone's Saga. I would certainly let a PC go through this effect at the climax of the personal story, if the player wants to. I just think it lame as a Rank 6 Gift instead of something else that could be more dramatically used than &quot;ok, I'm tired of this, I'll be Uktena now, folks&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T14:44:47-08:00","id":1157365,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1156706#post1156706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really something I'd ever allow a player to reach. Rank 6 is roughly as a 4th generation metuselah in your Vampire campaign... don't know, Karsh, Baba Yaga, Ur-Shulgi, Kementiri. And it really feels wrong to have a player handle the world that way. At that level of power and renown it's not even the same game, you'd better off playing Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157266#post1157266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm under the impression that for some reason you think that Rank 6 powers are bound to break the world like imba level 9 Vampire shit. Use your power, win the day, go home. But that's not the feeling the authors wanted to put in Werewolf nor the kind of power Rank 6 are supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Aren't these contradictory points though? At one point you said Rank 6 shouldn't be allowed because they are on par with 4th gen vampires, then state that Rank 6 isn't supposed to be at that level...or am I reading this wrong?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> As for Unstoppable Warrior, the Wendigo have Strength of Pine which is level 3, and it states that all physical damage on the character is healed by the next turn. So while its a powerful gift, there are other gifts out there that make it feel underwhelming. Toss in level 4 Shelter of Needles lets you spread that protection to allies as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T20:42:04-08:00","id":1157434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157328#post1157328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think about Firebringer, the more I wonder if pursuit of spiritual knowledge in general might be able to equal or exceed it. After all, there's a vast theoretical trove of untapped Gifts in old legends, Firebringer not required.</div> </div> </div> </div>A permissive storyteller may let you find any power in the Legendary realms. But maybe you have a ST more used to draw yellow tapes on what can be done, and the ability to steal &quot;warp reality&quot; from a Nexus Crawler or some Time magic from an Hermetic mage suddenly becomes invaluable. Assuming you can survive it first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, Dance of Shiva certainly is capable of breaking the world... it probably won't let you win, so much as flip the table that the board is on, though. And, again, Shield of Gaia is apparently more of an elder thing, since Darkwater Rokea learn C'et's Shell at Rank Five. </div> </div> </div>Gurhali can resurrect people with both a gift or a ritual (a level 3-4 one, if I remember) and there is no Garou power for that at all. The Fera are better at different things than the Garou, the fact that you're getting one of their most powerful gifts as a Rank 6 is actually pretty good. I don't know what Dance of Shiva does btw, where was it written? Has a W20 edition?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even level 9 Disciplines are not world breaking, they are a completely different level of gaming but world breaking, mmm no. Though I am against anything that makes a vamp look like a superhero. </div> </div> </div>Well... Dominate 9 lets you broadcast commands to every vampire descending from you and you're probably 1000 years old before you learn that power. It must be a generic order but &quot;Raze China to the ground&quot; is surely generic enough. Presence 9 lets you control the emotions &quot;in the entire city&quot;, can be used in torpor and can't be resisted through willpower. And the previous edition powers were even stronger...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157357#post1157357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep your lecture on the game to yourself, first and foremost. I got tired of it still in the 90's. I already know what the authors intended, what the game is supposed to do, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I so do not care. I'll write whatever I want, thank you very much, but feel free to never read or quote me should you feel so inclined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the question is those powers under the condition of being a Rank 6 Gift. Most of them are really cool ideas that could be explored in other ways. A Rank 6 Gift isn't simply a power. It is a power that: </div> </div> </div>1) Yes, that's why I think that Sleep of the Hero, for instance, is awesome. It has no combat or utility value, but story-wise it's astonishing.<br /> 2) I disagree. There's no reason to have something common and reintroduce it in a perfect version, even if a new thing might be more interesting.<br /> 3) Agreed, shouldn't be used all the time - except for the passive ones maybe. But it's better to customize them around the character rather than just learning them from a list (except something like Call the Great Fenris, that can be the kind of gift with a tradition inside the Tribe where &quot;only the greatest warriors can have the honor of...&quot;)<br /> 4) It mostly depends on the expectations of the player. The power should embody something they are or did, not just give them combat power.<br /> 5) A gift like Call the Great Fenris is extremely powerful and can be used. It also has a steep price that won't allow you to use it more than twice, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T22:36:23-08:00","id":1157465,"title":"","content":"Dance of Shiva is in the Nagah Breedbook. As I noted, it has a rather extreme swing on what it can do, from merely causing buildings to catch fire and burn down to incinerating most of the surface of the Earth for over 20 dice of aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T01:56:04-08:00","id":1157480,"title":"","content":"My personal suggestions on them:<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable Warrior</b>:<br /> What about it start downgrading every bit of non-silver damage? Agg becomes Lethal, Lethal becomes non-Lethal, and previously non-Lethal damage ceases to cause damage at all. Also, instead of regenerating with Rage, it could withstand with it, that is, the character spend Rage points to not take the unsoaked damage at all.<br /> <br /> <b>One on One</b>:<br /> It could cost you half your maximum Gnosis points, but no Perma.<br /> <br /> <b>Sleep of the Hero</b>:<br /> Make it a level 5 ritual, or even a level 4 ritual with specially stingy costs. Then the Gift could be Awaken the Hero to rouse those people from sleep on a time of crisis. So a Legendary Garou is the leader that will unite the heroes of the past when the tribe needs most.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller</b>:<br /> Some clarification on limits and possibilities would be interesting. I don't think it should be able to change past, for instance, but it could &quot;instinctively&quot; know if a given piece of the past is true enough to be used. So, lets say the Galliard wants to tell a tale of King Arthur returning from Avalon, the ST could veto this based on his need for no such thing ever happening at the past, but then the Garou gets to tell another thing, but if the ST don't have reason to not want an Arthur coming from Avalon, then the Garou got it right.<br /> <br /> <b>Call Great Fenris</b>:<br /> Instead of repeating the tale of Tyr, it could cost permanent Rage, as the Great Fenris remembers the character that the puny Rage of a Garou is nothing compared to his. Alternatively, it could have a requisite of extreme honesty to be used without a cost, and the risk of loosing one's hand could then be pending over the character's head without being a certainty.<br /> <br /> <b>Release from Bondage</b>:<br /> I see no reason to change it.<br /> <br /> <b>Firebringer</b>:<br /> At the very least, abdicating from defense seems silly to me. A Legendary hero could go the other way, becoming more resilient to each taken power. On the other hand, a simple way to better this one is to give the character a discount on XP to learn the same Gifts. Maybe even wave completely the cost until it amounts to the same cost of the Rank 6 Gift itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Home in All Lands</b>:<br /> Keep it as is.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Gaia</b>:<br /> It could be expanded to let in new immunity at a cost. Maybe similar to Firebringer in regard to the first exposition, and still limited to modern sources of damage, or even to only industrialized sources of damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Renew the Cycle</b>:<br /> I would rewrite this thing entirely. I'll post what I did to it later. The fluff is awesome, but killing vampires simply isn't that great or silverfangish.<br /> <br /> <b>Thought-Form of the Twelve Ministers</b>:<br /> No change.<br /> <br /> <b>Invoked Presence</b>:<br /> Could be broken down in specific gifts for the presence of each Totem.<br /> <br /> <b>As In the Beginning</b>:<br /> Needs to do what is supposed to do. Reduce the local Gauntlet to 0 during a scene, and add more specific rules on the area affected.<br /> <br /> <b>Rebirthing</b>:<br /> Is a good thing for Grimfang. It don't need to be stated as a Gift, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Becoming Uktena</b>:<br /> Also something to take out from the list as a Gift. It could be interesting as a ritual, as a special Fetish, or as a special event without hard rules attached.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T10:41:11-08:00","id":1157592,"title":"","content":"<b>Unstoppable Warrior</b>:<br /> Roll Rage difficulty 6 at the beginning of every turn, you regenerate that much damage, even from silver, at the end of the turn even if you have taken enough damage to take you beyond incapacitated. The effects of the gift are permanent.<br /> <br /> <b>One on One</b>:<br /> The gift may be used only at night time when the moon is visible in the night sky. The cost to activate it depends on the phase of the moon: 2 for full moon, 3 for gibbous, 4 for half, 5 for crescent, may not be used on the nights of new moon.<br /> <br /> <b>Sleep of the Hero</b>:<br /> The Hero will always return when Gaia demands it, be it for a caern in danger, to resque an important character, defeat an impossible threat or whatever dramatic reason. The hero will remain until his goal is succeeded or failed. The gift automatically activates once per story when the story teller feels its right to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller</b>:<br /> The Galliard must say the story to an audience and must know firsthand the events, if the story has never been true in the first place may never be altered, if the story is based on true events with real persons he may alter it as he pleases, when the story telling ends the events of the story changed for real as well, how that affects the row of history is something the Galliard has to discover for himself.<br /> <br /> <b>Call Great Fenris</b>:<br /> The avatar of great Fenris has no stats, does aggravated usoakable damage and may not be damaged by any means except from entities of the same level. If the hero who summoned it does not perform in the combat up to his fullest potential, aka does not satisfy the spirit's expectations, will be devoured.<br /> <br /> <b>Release from Bondage</b>:<br /> The werewolf may not be bonded by any means, instead of gaining 15 strength for that purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Firebringer</b>:<br /> Enemies gain no modifier for a power used on the garou, normal difficulty applies, though the power in question must be used successfully upon the Ragabash and suffer its effects. Then he learns automatically the power of the gift and may use it against his foes, he can also teach these powers as gifts to other garou, also may teach any gift he knows as if he was a spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Home in All Lands</b>:<br /> Keep it as is.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Gaia</b>:<br /> Automatically works on any crafted, no natural source of damage, be it bombs, laser beams, bullets etc etc. The gift will not work against natural sources of damage, if you throw a rock it still applies normal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Renew the Cycle</b>:<br /> Call it Return to Gaia's Cycle, the gift is the bane of all things that should be dead but are not, be it vampires, mummys, warlocks etc etc. The more ancient the offender of Gaia's cycle the more easy is the roll of the gift activation and more dramatic the effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Invoked Presence</b>:<br /> The gift invokes the Tribal Totem or a celestine he is allied/in favor with, the effects of the gift are up to the story teller and are even more powerful than full powered Totem Gift (metis). When the gift ends the mighty spirit takes the werewolf with it and demands a chiminage to prove his worth before using the gift again.<br /> <br /> <b>As In the Beginning</b>:<br /> The Theurge not only reduces gauntlet to 0 but actually merges the spiritual with the material world, spirits unite with their material counterparts and gain their true ancient forms, the union of spirit and flesh gives to living creatures supernatural properties, they add their spirit Rage willpower and Gnosis to their respected stats, they soak aggravated damage and regenerate lethal like garou, they become highly intelligent and may communicate with people. Other spiritual entities like gaia, luna or helios may assist the werewolf depending on circumstances.<br /> <br /> <b>Rebirthing</b>:<br /> No need to be born again from a mother's womb, the werewolf, dies leaves bones behind and reshapes in the umbra at an age that would resemble a freshly changed cub.<br /> <br /> <b>Becoming Uktena</b>:<br /> Remove the forever transformation, the werewolf though may be in danger to lose himself to the raw power of the gift and really think that he is uktena for ever. The Uktena stats are added to the unmodified homid attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T12:42:31-08:00","id":1157614,"title":"","content":"<b>Gift of Power (Rank 6 general gift):</b><br /> Win the game. Congratulation, you've just won at Werewolf!<br /> <br /> There, I fixed your underpowered gifts. No thanks needed. And now I'm out. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T15:25:57-08:00","id":1157646,"title":"","content":"The narrative purpose of Rank, Arete, Dharma etc are completely at odds with the narrative purpose of Generation. For any and all power a Rank Six CB has it does not hold the same narrative purpose in werewolf as any form of Elder Kindred and trying to compare them powerwise misses the purpose except in that at best Vampire Blood gods are Midbosses in the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> The Malfean Lords are written up with ways to defeat them permanently that's exactly the sort of thing Rank six does. CB are expected to gain power. Now they might fail along the way but unlike Generation there is a natural growth between ranks. Generation must be stolen and at great cost, it is a forbidden thing that the game goes out of its way to make hard to achieve, and generally kindred society frowns on it. Conversely generally Rank gain is supposed by the acts of CB society. IT is expected a Rank 1 will some day be rank 3. It is never expected a 13th gen will ever be an 11th.<br /> <br /> Now 5 to 6 is a jump for only the highest of games but so what? If you really have issue with power go play a bunch of parapalegics who are mentally challenged who get 1s in all traits and no supernatural powers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T00:13:29-08:00","id":1157707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157646#post1157646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> CB</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a CB? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T06:34:28-08:00","id":1157736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157614#post1157614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gift of Power (Rank 6 general gift):</b><br /> Win the game. Congratulation, you've just won at Werewolf!<br /> <br /> There, I fixed your underpowered gifts. No thanks needed. And now I'm out. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually gave me an idea. A general rule on Rank 6 Gifts.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 6 Gift (Unique):</b><br /> At the pinnacle of your journey, you was personally gifted by a Celestine. The entity coalesced your own destiny in the archetypal manifestation of your spiritual power.<br /> <br /> Give a name and concept to your personal Gift, discussing it with your ST. Once per scene you can declare an effect on the scope of the Gift and what each success will mean in a pure Gnosis roll. A single success can exact the same effect a lesser Gift would at 5 successes, for example, while additional successes multiply variables like range or duration. Costs are halved for each Rank of difference between the original effect and 6 (1 Perma dot becomes 5 temp points, 1 temp point becomes 0). If the effect calls for a resisted roll, it is done with either Willpower, Gnosis or Rage with +5 dice and 1 additional success on your result.<br /> <br /> The ST can let you improvise effects at higher costs. As a rule of thumb, any effect able to alter the status of a battlefield should cost 1 to 5 points of either Willpower, Rage or Gnosis. An effect that can change the status in a big caern and its territory should cost 1 permanent dot, +1 per other caerns affected. An effect that can change the course of history should cost your character in a way or another, but should be truly epic.<br /> <br /> You can't call those effects for naught, though. Rank 6 Gift is a personal bless from one of the greatest spirits, and a manifestation of your very essence and destiny. Using it for lesser tasks or without good reason can mess with your being and fate, always to achieve the greatness you deserve. The first symptoms seem like ill luck, making those uses result in a big chain of unintended events. If still abused, fate causes even more trouble, as it leads you to hard situations that justify the use of such gifts. The bad luck goes on until the untimely end of the legendary hero in a way fitting to the great stories of the People. Depending on the Garou in question, the spirits can try to warn of such fate before it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T06:55:41-08:00","id":1157738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157646#post1157646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative purpose of Rank, Arete, Dharma etc are completely at odds with the narrative purpose of Generation. For any and all power a Rank Six CB has it does not hold the same narrative purpose in werewolf as any form of Elder Kindred and trying to compare them powerwise misses the purpose except in that at best Vampire Blood gods are Midbosses in the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> The Malfean Lords are written up with ways to defeat them permanently that's exactly the sort of thing Rank six does. CB are expected to gain power. Now they might fail along the way but unlike Generation there is a natural growth between ranks. Generation must be stolen and at great cost, it is a forbidden thing that the game goes out of its way to make hard to achieve, and generally kindred society frowns on it. Conversely generally Rank gain is supposed by the acts of CB society. IT is expected a Rank 1 will some day be rank 3. It is never expected a 13th gen will ever be an 11th.<br /> <br /> Now 5 to 6 is a jump for only the highest of games but so what? If you really have issue with power go play a bunch of parapalegics who are mentally challenged who get 1s in all traits and no supernatural powers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would only add that great vampires are midbosses from an exclusively CB lines standpoint. Once you go for a true cross-over it becomes a muddy question. But regardless, for all WtA purposes that is a pretty valid point. Generation works on a game paradigm completely distinct from Rank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157707#post1157707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a CB? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T07:54:27-08:00","id":1157752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157646#post1157646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generation must be stolen and at great cost, it is a forbidden thing that the game goes out of its way to make hard to achieve, and generally kindred society frowns on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only true in a Camarilla campaign. Sabbat and Independents have less to none social stigma for it and Assamites are actually encouraged to lower their generation.<br /> There was this guy playing in a game shop that once said &quot;Oh yea I finally reached 5th generation! But it was hard, I've been playing this character for nearly three months!&quot;. So you look at him, smile and get away, because... well, kids be kids. Teenagers are all about dreams of power playing and feeling superhuman, but if you read enough by when you reach your thirties you begin to see how cheap is that kind of narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now 5 to 6 is a jump for only the highest of games but so what? If you really have issue with power go play a bunch of parapalegics who are mentally challenged who get 1s in all traits and no supernatural powers! </div> </div> </div>Woosh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T08:17:17-08:00","id":1157756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157752#post1157752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only true in a Camarilla campaign. Sabbat and Independents have less to none social stigma for it and Assamites are actually encouraged to lower their generation.<br /> There was this guy playing in a game shop that once said &quot;Oh yea I finally reached 5th generation! But it was hard, I've been playing this character for nearly three months!&quot;. So you look at him, smile and get away, because... well, kids be kids. Teenagers are all about dreams of power playing and feeling superhuman, but if you read enough by when you reach your thirties you begin to see how cheap is that kind of narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even withing groups where it is acceptable, Diablerie isn't an easy thing. You still have to play nice to a degree, so you don't piss people off more than you should, and getting to the throats of those elders is usually far harder than it seems. It stands that rising Generation is possible, but out-of-the-way in Vampire, while rising Rank is expected in Werewolf. Both are possible, but evoke fairly distinct themes and decisions.<br /> <br /> About how cheap is a teenager bragging on power, what else isn't cheap when you're a teenager? Vampire was born out of teenagers wanting to be Dark &amp; Gritty &amp; Angst against the System. It is still a good game, and can be maturely played. Let kids be kids, and let grown-ups be kids when they want. By the way, I knew a guy who played a 5th gen Assamite, but it was after 5 years of play. I had a 5th gen character a couple of times, but those started the game on this generation, I almost never raised gen in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:06:24-08:00","id":1157777,"title":"","content":"Can we restart talking about Garou ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T18:06:44-08:00","id":1157842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157777#post1157777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we restart talking about Garou ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so. Is there any opinions on my write-up for general rule on Rank 6?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T22:09:31-08:00","id":1157875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157752#post1157752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only true in a Camarilla campaign. Sabbat and Independents have less to none social stigma for it and Assamites are actually encouraged to lower their generation.<br /> There was this guy playing in a game shop that once said &quot;Oh yea I finally reached 5th generation! But it was hard, I've been playing this character for nearly three months!&quot;. So you look at him, smile and get away, because... well, kids be kids. Teenagers are all about dreams of power playing and feeling superhuman, but if you read enough by when you reach your thirties you begin to see how cheap is that kind of narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the only thing that really changes in your 30s is that you don't really have time to play very much any more. And that you might also forget that teenagers and 20-somethings can often fit in time when you didn't think to, so the three months of play time might constitute and extremely dense block of meet-ups and scene clusters. Sometimes, games also have to be high-powered to answer questions involving the use of power, such as with Exalted. It's generally writ a bit smaller in WoD games, but then, WoD games have also had a bad track record of QC when it comes to tuning powers to an intended level. Kiai 6 is a very good example, while at the other end, there's Razor Claws, arguably even after its W20 adjustment. It'd be nice to have first rank Gifts be where they are way more from affinity than from some kind of assumed &quot;ground floor power level, start here&quot; assumption. Zero to hero is not something that needs to be the assumed play style of every game.<br /> <br /> (Quite frankly, if I were backing away from the group, the reasoning would start and end at &quot;they play Vampire&quot;, because that's just not for me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T22:12:29-08:00","id":1157876,"title":"","content":"I think that the idea of a legend gaining a legendary power that has something to do with the legend it's very much on point. You leave your mark in the spirit world and the spirit world marks you in return.<br /> <br /> Not so the &quot;invent what you want on the fly&quot; thing. It departs from what Gifts are (a power the spirits give to you). Besides, a Legend it's someone who has done great deeds without the lvl 6, they shouldn't need &quot;magick(tm)&quot; to change the story.<br /> <br /> Instead make so Rank 6 it's such a big social boost that you barely need Chriminage with Gaian spirits, everyone understands that if a Legend says something has to be done, it has to be done. Incarna are happy to have you in their courts as advisor and ally. NO spirit it's ever going to deny you a Gift, even if they are of other Tribes.<br /> <br /> Also more lvl 6 powers could be rewarded if the character keeps doing Epic stuff. <hr /><br /> I don't get Maris complaints. I don't like power gamers that want lvl 6 to increase their &quot;ass kicking algorithm&quot;, but why should a Legendary power be less than earthshaking?, what does THAT add to the Legend from a ST point of view? .<br /> <br /> In my opinion Lvl 6 powers are suposed to be Epic, that being said Epic isn't always &quot;nice&quot; -<br /> <br /> Becoming Uktena does Epic very well. Sure, it &quot;kills you&quot; at the end of the scene, but it also gives you narrative powers limited by the ST (and they should be massively powerful powers, since <a href=\"http://www.wyrmfoe.com/1577/becoming-uktena/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;even a Thunderwyrm should fear you&quot;</a>) during that scene. I think such epic powers should change the result of said scene, and doing the impossible before dying it's a very cool way to retire your character. In a sense, it IS an &quot;I won werewolf button&quot;, but done in a very thematic way. Thus I don't think it sucks, far from it, it's the perfect stuff to give a Legend (a way to &quot;die&quot; with awesomeness).<br /> The link says it's &quot;frustrating&quot; that they don't give mechanics to this thing. I don't see this as &quot;frustrating&quot; at all. It's not casual either. It's because such an epic moment shouldnt be ruined with stats and checks. It would be like giving stats to Ur-Shulgi, an Antediluvian, or an Incarna-I would rather not do that.<br /> <br /> Others, like the &quot;ash a vampire thing&quot;, if not necessarily weak, they surely look underwhelming to me and I wouldn't mind to change them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-12-2017, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T04:43:12-08:00","id":1157907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157736#post1157736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 6 Gift (Unique):</b><br /> At the pinnacle of your journey, you was personally gifted by a Celestine. The entity coalesced your own destiny in the archetypal manifestation of your spiritual power.<br /> <br /> Give a name and concept to your personal Gift, discussing it with your ST. Once per scene you can declare an effect on the scope of the Gift and what each success will mean in a pure Gnosis roll. A single success can exact the same effect a lesser Gift would at 5 successes, for example, while additional successes multiply variables like range or duration. Costs are halved for each Rank of difference between the original effect and 6 (1 Perma dot becomes 5 temp points, 1 temp point becomes 0). If the effect calls for a resisted roll, it is done with either Willpower, Gnosis or Rage with +5 dice and 1 additional success on your result.<br /> <br /> The ST can let you improvise effects at higher costs. As a rule of thumb, any effect able to alter the status of a battlefield should cost 1 to 5 points of either Willpower, Rage or Gnosis. An effect that can change the status in a big caern and its territory should cost 1 permanent dot, +1 per other caerns affected. An effect that can change the course of history should cost your character in a way or another, but should be truly epic.<br /> <br /> You can't call those effects for naught, though. Rank 6 Gift is a personal bless from one of the greatest spirits, and a manifestation of your very essence and destiny. Using it for lesser tasks or without good reason can mess with your being and fate, always to achieve the greatness you deserve. The first symptoms seem like ill luck, making those uses result in a big chain of unintended events. If still abused, fate causes even more trouble, as it leads you to hard situations that justify the use of such gifts. The bad luck goes on until the untimely end of the legendary hero in a way fitting to the great stories of the People. Depending on the Garou in question, the spirits can try to warn of such fate before it's too late.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 2nd and the 3rd paragraph remind me Mage rather than Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Appart from that a rank 6 gift may, or may not, have anything to do with destiny, gifts that call upon the favor of celestines may indeed force their wrath upon a bad user of their blessings, like calling Helios to bake the bacon and eggs you have just put on your car's bonnet. On the other hand there might be a use of a rank 6 gift for lesser tasks that will actually end up to a great benefit for Gaia, that of course might make the celestine invoked to question the werewolve's reasons for his power's abuse and that actually might be a great story theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T08:58:19-08:00","id":1157943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157876#post1157876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the idea of a legend gaining a legendary power that has something to do with the legend it's very much on point. You leave your mark in the spirit world and the spirit world marks you in return.<br /> <br /> Not so the &quot;invent what you want on the fly&quot; thing. It departs from what Gifts are (a power the spirits give to you). Besides, a Legend it's someone who has done great deeds without the lvl 6, they shouldn't need &quot;magick(tm)&quot; to change the story.<br /> <br /> Instead make so Rank 6 it's such a big social boost that you barely need Chriminage with Gaian spirits, everyone understands that if a Legend says something has to be done, it has to be done. Incarna are happy to have you in their courts as advisor and ally. NO spirit it's ever going to deny you a Gift, even if they are of other Tribes.<br /> <br /> Also more lvl 6 powers could be rewarded if the character keeps doing Epic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>My goal is to have a guideline for creation of custom Gifts instead of a list of examples that will be used much like other Ranks lists. I'll try again, and implement your considerations, I agree with them on a second look (it was just a first draft), and I liked the social bonus idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157876#post1157876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get Maris complaints. I don't like power gamers that want lvl 6 to increase their &quot;ass kicking algorithm&quot;, but why should a Legendary power be less than earthshaking?, what does THAT add to the Legend from a ST point of view? .<br /> <br /> In my opinion Lvl 6 powers are suposed to be Epic, that being said Epic isn't always &quot;nice&quot; -<br /> <br /> Becoming Uktena does Epic very well. Sure, it &quot;kills you&quot; at the end of the scene, but it also gives you narrative powers limited by the ST (and they should be massively powerful powers, since <a href=\"http://www.wyrmfoe.com/1577/becoming-uktena/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;even a Thunderwyrm should fear you&quot;</a>) during that scene. I think such epic powers should change the result of said scene, and doing the impossible before dying it's a very cool way to retire your character. In a sense, it IS an &quot;I won werewolf button&quot;, but done in a very thematic way. Thus I don't think it sucks, far from it, it's the perfect stuff to give a Legend (a way to &quot;die&quot; with awesomeness).<br /> The link says it's &quot;frustrating&quot; that they don't give mechanics to this thing. I don't see this as &quot;frustrating&quot; at all. It's not casual either. It's because such an epic moment shouldnt be ruined with stats and checks. It would be like giving stats to Ur-Shulgi, an Antediluvian, or an Incarna-I would rather not do that.<br /> <br /> Others, like the &quot;ash a vampire thing&quot;, if not necessarily weak, they surely look underwhelming to me and I wouldn't mind to change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my complaint with Becoming Uktena is more on line with it being mechanically a Gift than the idea itself. Though it did gave me another idea for the next iteration of Rank 6.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157907#post1157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The 2nd and the 3rd paragraph remind me Mage rather than Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Appart from that a rank 6 gift may, or may not, have anything to do with destiny, gifts that call upon the favor of celestines may indeed force their wrath upon a bad user of their blessings, like calling Helios to bake the bacon and eggs you have just put on your car's bonnet. On the other hand there might be a use of a rank 6 gift for lesser tasks that will actually end up to a great benefit for Gaia, that of course might make the celestine invoked to question the werewolve's reasons for his power's abuse and that actually might be a great story theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as that works fine for lesser Gifts, a Rank 6 should be more attuned to the specific character than anything else, hence my take on it being linked to personal destiny. Until Rank 5, Gifts are &quot;just&quot; the favor of spirits upon the Changer. But now this guy is a Legend by all means, so it should be as much the Celestine giving favor as guiding the legend itself to settle. Also, you already have for &quot;lesser&quot; Changers the watching eyes of the spirits, a Legend shouldn't be someone who needs a babysitter. So, instead of imposing limits through the wrath of gods (something this Garou is already powerful enough to face), I wanted to dial up the idea of your actions having consequences. A Legend is so powerful that even the simplest actions can ripple into world-shaking events if done without the proper consideration, specially if implementing such signature powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, so lemme do it again:<br /> <b>Rank 6 Gift (Unique):</b><br /> Reaching the pinnacle of your journey, you was personally gifted by a Celestine. The entity coalesced your own destiny in the archetypal manifestation of your spiritual power.<br /> <br /> Give a name and concept to your personal Gift, discussing it with your ST. If it evolves from a lesser Gift, a single success can exact the same effect the lesser Gift would at 5 successes, for example, while additional successes each double variables like range or duration. Costs are halved for each Rank of difference between the original effect and 6 (1 Perma dot becomes 5 temp points, 1 temp point becomes 0). If the effect calls for a resisted roll, it is done with either Willpower, Gnosis or Rage with +5 dice and 1 additional success on your result.<br /> <br /> You can create unique higher effects. As a rule of thumb, any effect able to alter the status of a battlefield should cost 1 to 5 points of either Willpower, Rage or Gnosis. An effect that can change the status in a big caern and its territory should cost 1 permanent dot, +1 per other caerns affected. You roll either Gnosis, Rage or Willpower for non-resisted effects, and with +5 for resisted. It is a rough guideline, and you should work with your ST the details.<br /> <br /> Along with those stated effects, every Rank 6 Gift also have a constant effect for interaction with spirits and a single-use effect called a Call to Destiny. The effect on spirits rouses from you being recognized both as a favored of a Celestine and a powerful Legend by yourself. Most spirits recognize you on spot, and any below Incarna will defer to you out of respect or fear if not coerced by other powerful beings. You never have to roll against those spirits, but you can have to roll against their master's influence (you get a -2 dif. in the roll if the master isn't felt present by the spirit in question). Greater spirits still respect you as equal to the lesser among the Incarnae, so even the greatest Tribal Totems will at least pay attention to you and heed you advice. Some can go as far as to challenge others for the right to have you as a counselor.<br /> <br /> Call to Destiny is the ultimate effect a Werewolf can expect to achieve in life. It can come in two flavors: Sacrificial Destiny or Guarded for Destiny. A Sacrificial Destiny lets you access the full power of a deity for a brief time. You can call Great Fenris in its full glory to the Battlefield, or become the very Uktena, mingle permanently with the mind of Queen Ananasa, or curse a single place with the very presence of Wendigo forever. Whatever you do, your character is gone for the player. The deed can have lasting effects, but no hard rules are necessary on the creation of the Gift, just the way the character will leave play.<br /> <br /> If you choose a Guarded Destiny, instead you state a way for the Gift to save you from an untimely death. It can be used only once, and can't save you from a Sacrificial Destiny, but can save you from threats you couldn't overcome with all your Legendary might. Most Legends have a single Guarded Destiny, if any, to strike back in the same battle. You also choose a Legendary Scar to mark you once the Guarded Destiny was used.<br /> <br /> Only one Call to Destiny can be used in the entire character's life, but new Gifts can expand on the descriptive options when the time has come. When you trigger the Call to Destiny, you can mix all your Rank 6 Gifts in the final effect as you want, only keeping the limit of not causing the damage of a Sacrificial Destiny at the same time that you use a Guarded Destiny (tough you can use other effects of the Gift that grants the Sacrificial Destiny and mix its effects in the narrative of the return).<br /> <br /> Rank 6 Gift is a personal bless from one of the greatest spirits, and a manifestation of your very essence and destiny. Using it for lesser tasks or without good reason can mess with your being and fate, always to achieve the greatness you deserve. The first symptoms seem like ill luck, making those uses result in a big chain of unintended events. If still abused, fate causes even more trouble, as it leads you to hard situations that justify the use of such gifts. The bad luck goes on until the untimely end of the legendary hero in a way fitting to the great stories of the People. Depending on the Garou in question, the spirits can try to warn of such fate before it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T11:06:28-08:00","id":1157964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157943#post1157943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, so lemme do it again:<br /> <b>Rank 6 Gift (Unique):</b><br /> Reaching the pinnacle of your journey, you was personally gifted by a Celestine. The entity coalesced your own destiny in the archetypal manifestation of your spiritual power.<br /> <br /> Give a name and concept to your personal Gift, discussing it with your ST. If it evolves from a lesser Gift, a single success can exact the same effect the lesser Gift would at 5 successes, for example, while additional successes each double variables like range or duration. Costs are halved for each Rank of difference between the original effect and 6 (1 Perma dot becomes 5 temp points, 1 temp point becomes 0). If the effect calls for a resisted roll, it is done with either Willpower, Gnosis or Rage with +5 dice and 1 additional success on your result.<br /> <br /> You can create unique higher effects. As a rule of thumb, any effect able to alter the status of a battlefield should cost 1 to 5 points of either Willpower, Rage or Gnosis. An effect that can change the status in a big caern and its territory should cost 1 permanent dot, +1 per other caerns affected. You roll either Gnosis, Rage or Willpower for non-resisted effects, and with +5 for resisted. It is a rough guideline, and you should work with your ST the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I am fan of uniqueness, and definately a rank 6 gift might look like a maximized effect from a lesser gift, like the beloved to all Unstoppable Warrior resemblance to Combat Healing, though the successes restriction, or the buying cost is not something I would follow. I tend to keep closer to maintream book stuff. I would lean towards the challenge to create a unique gift in theme and system rather than creating a strict universal system on how to create Rank 6 gifts, but thats a personal taking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157943#post1157943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call to Destiny</div> </div> </div> </div>This concept reminds me Rackham confrontation's Champions of Destiny or something like that. The champions of fate in this game never really die and even if they do they can be brought back to life again and again.<br /> <a href=\"http://underthemountainblog.com/athenaeum/aarklash-archive/factions/wolfen-of-yllia/\" target=\"_blank\">http://underthemountainblog.com/athe...lfen-of-yllia/</a><br /> <br /> If fate is a major thing to a setting, fine by me, if players think that fate should not be too much of a prerequisite for a rank 6 gift or relationship with a celestine, then you can simply remove it.<br /> On the other side of the coin fate may be something that you can add or remove from a rank six hero depending on the drama of a story, but when it is indeed added to a story it must be resolved at any cost. It should be THAT serious.<br /> <br /> The sure thing about Rank 6 is to create an awesomely unique individual with equally awesome dramatic background, like a hero that he is the lover to a moon or star deity and thus may never find complete delight to matterial pleasures he so thoroughly misses, being kept away from the world of flesh by his mistress or lord to a monster tha is so consumed by Rage and bloodlust that he may never crave for any other emotion, keeping away all those who still care and love him/ her. Rank 6 status is not only about Power. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Examples</b></u><br /> Jonas Albrecht is the Silver Fang King that will never rule the Garou nation, but destined to always Lead it in battle.<br /> Yuri the Margrave, is the fitting Ruler of the Garou nation that will never rule it, but destined to guide it unwillingly back to their Silver Fang Lords.<br /> Golgol Fangs First is the Warlorld of Amazon, destined to win the battle but never leave its battlefield.<br /> Grim Fang has gained great knowledge over many lives and will always be the greatest mentor of the Garou nation but he is destined to die from the greatest threats that befall upon the Garou, never witnessing the greatest victories, or changes that happen to the world from garou actions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-12-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T12:16:27-08:00","id":1157976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157964#post1157964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I am fan of uniqueness, and definately a rank 6 gift might look like a maximized effect from a lesser gift, like the beloved to all Unstoppable Warrior resemblance to Combat Healing, though the successes restriction, or the buying cost is not something I would follow. I tend to keep closer to maintream book stuff. I would lean towards the challenge to create a unique gift in theme and system rather than creating a strict universal system on how to create Rank 6 gifts, but thats a personal taking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This concept reminds me Rackham confrontation's Champions of Destiny or something like that. The champions of fate in this game never really die and even if they do they can be brought back to life again and again.<br /> <a href=\"http://underthemountainblog.com/athenaeum/aarklash-archive/factions/wolfen-of-yllia/\" target=\"_blank\">http://underthemountainblog.com/athe...lfen-of-yllia/</a><br /> <br /> If fate is a major thing to a setting, fine by me, if players think that fate should not be too much of a prerequisite for a rank 6 gift or relationship with a celestine, then you can simply remove it.<br /> On the other side of the coin fate may be something that you can add or remove from a rank six hero depending on the drama of a story, but when it is indeed added to a story it must be resolved at any cost. It should be THAT serious.<br /> <br /> The sure thing about Rank 6 is to create an awesomely unique individual with equally awesome dramatic background, like a hero that he is the lover to a moon or star deity and thus may never find complete delight to matterial pleasures he so thoroughly misses, being kept away from the world of flesh by his mistress or lord to a monster tha is so consumed by Rage and bloodlust that he may never crave for any other emotion, keeping away all those who still care and love him/ her. Rank 6 status is not only about Power.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Examples</b></u><br /> Jonas Albrecht is the Silver Fang King that will never rule the Garou nation, but destined to always Lead it in battle.<br /> Yuri the Margrave, is the fitting Ruler of the Garou nation that will never rule it, but destined to guide it unwillingly back to their Silver Fang Lords.<br /> Golgol Fangs First is the Warlorld of Amazon, destined to win the battle but never leave its battlefield.<br /> Grim Fang has gained great knowledge over many lives and will always be the greatest mentor of the Garou nation but he is destined to die from the greatest threats that befall upon the Garou, never witnessing the greatest victories, or changes that happen to the world from garou actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the feeling about unique mechanics, and I think both approaches could coexist without more of a problem.<br /> <br /> On the Destiny thing, I understand the worry, but I wanted to limit a little what would be acquired just from one aspect. What other rules or material could be there for Rank 6 characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T02:30:46-08:00","id":1158114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1157976#post1157976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other rules or material could be there for Rank 6 characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets sum up what we have gathered so far and add up what we may come in mind further.<br /> a) Special backgrounds and merits.<br /> b) Attributes and skills above 5, maybe maximum 6, or even further.<br /> c) Unique Rank 6 gifts.<br /> d) Unique celestine- incarna relationship.<br /> e) Epic destiny.<br /> f) Epic story elements and cocepts, the mother of all battles, the endless planeswalking, the neverending journey of wisdom, the myth slayer, the love savior, the dream guardian etc etc etc.<br /> g) Special social bonuses.<br /> h) Special frenzy bonuses.<br /> i) Level 6 Fetish<br /> <br /> Hmm what else ....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-13-2017, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T06:37:13-08:00","id":1158157,"title":"","content":"I like the new version.<br /> <br /> As for those ideas:<br /> a) Merits are already &quot;special&quot; by definition. I don't think that the act of gaining Rank 6 should give you a new Merit (unless it's part of the Gift), but rather I would say that any Werewolf that has lived trough all the ordeals and Umbra travel that would be required to become a Legend probably picked up a supernatural Merit or two along the road, merely by interacting with the supernatural world.<br /> A special Background could be more reasonable, but instead I suggest allowing supernatural Backgrounds (like Ancestors) above 5 (and to suggest that probably Legends have backgrounds above 5 representing the influence over the supernatural world or the mundane world that they have earned trough their deeds).<br /> b) I wouldn't give this because Garou can get this through Totems, Fetishes and Gifts (and far beyond 6), one doesn't need to use vampire rules for all settings, unless the legendary Gift itself provides a permanent increase in atributes<br /> c) Sure<br /> d) Sure, in fact, it could be a prerequisite to get to Rank 6<br /> e) Probably, if they don't have one, they sure can forge one. Hey, you could take a page out of Mage and give Destiny 5 as the &quot;special Background&quot; for a), at the players choice<br /> f)absolutely<br /> g)Suggested this one<br /> h) Not bad.<br /> <br /> Shining so bright in the spirit world could also get you the unwanted attentions of the Wyrm: The Maeljin also know your name. Potent Wyrm entities may be out to get you. Though, again, this may be better as a result of your path to the Rank 6 (if you went so far, sure you have defeated the wyrm in many ocasions) rather than an effect of the Rank itself.<br /> <br /> 1 more idea. Rank can be given posthumously. In this case achieving Rank 6 could include to be at the receiving end of a Sleep of the Hero effect (be it from a Ritual casted as part of the ceremony or an effect of dying in such good graces with Gaia)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T08:04:23-08:00","id":1158168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1158157#post1158157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the new version.<br /> <br /> Shining so bright in the spirit world could also get you the unwanted attentions of the Wyrm: The Maeljin also know your name. Potent Wyrm entities may be out to get you. Though, again, this may be better as a result of your path to the Rank 6 (if you went so far, sure you have defeated the wyrm in many ocasions) rather than an effect of the Rank itself.<br /> <br /> 1 more idea. Rank can be given posthumously. In this case achieving Rank 6 could include to be at the receiving end of a Sleep of the Hero effect (be it from a Ritual casted as part of the ceremony or an effect of dying in such good graces with Gaia)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> Or become a powerful ancestor feared by the Wyrm. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T18:59:55-08:00","id":1158315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1158114#post1158114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets sum up what we have gathered so far and add up what we may come in mind further.<br /> a) Special backgrounds and merits.<br /> b) Attributes and skills above 5, maybe maximum 6, or even further.<br /> c) Unique Rank 6 gifts.<br /> d) Unique celestine- incarna relationship.<br /> e) Epic destiny.<br /> f) Epic story elements and cocepts, the mother of all battles, the endless planeswalking, the neverending journey of wisdom, the myth slayer, the love savior, the dream guardian etc etc etc.<br /> g) Special social bonuses.<br /> h) Special frenzy bonuses.<br /> i) Level 6 Fetish<br /> <br /> Hmm what else ....</div> </div> </div> </div>A) Guide to Technocracy already worked on the above lvl 5 BG, and I'm not very fond of those rules, though they were for pooling BG. They mostly take the BG to another level of OP in narrative without adding nothing really of interest to the game. Instead, we could do the middle ground: new BGs based on the &quot;natural progression&quot; of common BGs, but with distinct rules to fine-tune how it really affects the game. I'll take a look in a WoD BGs list later to start organizing some ideas, or someone could do that.<br /> <br /> B) Though I'll go with <b>Aleph</b> on this, I do think some Gifts to permanently increase Attributes can be a good idea. Some legends <u>are</u> about impressive levels of &quot;natural qualities&quot;, like the strength 8 in Homid of Zhizhak.<br /> <br /> C) Well, we're working on it.<br /> <br /> D) Again, I like <b>Aleph</b>'s idea of it as a requisite. We could write up some examples, and the kind of spirit quests needed to achieve such relationship.<br /> <br /> E) Need some streamlined ruled on this, though. I'll take a look at Mage's Destiny later.<br /> <br /> F) I'm thinking on wrapping the other elements around this one. You personal concept or epic calling defines what you get as a Legend.<br /> <br /> G) Did some, already, as Aleph proposed, but can we add others? It could work in a similar manner to Pure Breed, maybe? I think so since this BG is already described as a spiritual resemblance to heroes of old. Pure Breed could attain an entirely new level of meaning for a Legend. And maybe the old Pure Breed should be replaced by such characters, since it doesn't matter anymore to whom in the past they have a semblance. They are the Great Heroes themselves, now.<br /> <br /> H) Certainly. Until Elder Rank got you to be ever harder to frenzy. At the level of a Legend you could be simply beyond such concerns. Maybe instead of normal Frenzy rules, you should roll to keep yourself from loosing control of the consequences of your actions. I don't imagine a Legend entering Frenzy if it doesn't want nor was cursed to do so, but just being a little upset could make it step a little beyond the line.<br /> <br /> I) Fetishes of such level should be legendary by themselves, so as much as it is interesting, it is something to make with some caution. At least they should be as unique as the Gifts, or even more.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers and other minions of the Wyrm, if not the Hydra itself, should be as affected as any other by the Legendary status. I did thought it through when making my little rule. Spirits of the Wyrm would still listen and obey a Legend out of sheer terror and respect for such prowess, unless directed by the greater horrors of their masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T02:12:11-08:00","id":1158393,"title":"","content":"Another thing that makes me wonder is how to find ways in order to aleviate the horror theme of werewolf the apocalypse up to the rank 6 level for both character and campaign mood.<br /> My personal experience with our characters is that they turm more alien with every rank, monstrous, otherworldly, mysterious, unpredictable, inhuman. The character has no feelings for mankind, only for universal balance at any means necessary. Taking lives, destroying cities, preventing technological progress etc etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:09:33-08:00","id":1158608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1158393#post1158393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that makes me wonder is how to find ways in order to aleviate the horror theme of werewolf the apocalypse up to the rank 6 level for both character and campaign mood.<br /> My personal experience with our characters is that they turm more alien with every rank, monstrous, otherworldly, mysterious, unpredictable, inhuman. The character has no feelings for mankind, only for universal balance at any means necessary. Taking lives, destroying cities, preventing technological progress etc etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really have to ask yourself if this jives with maintaining all Renown at 10 dots, because it feels like it wouldn't be very conducive to it, nor would it make the character the ne plus ultra of what they represent that legendary Rank entails. The horror, as far as Werewolf is concerned when it utilizes its particular horror genre conventions, is that the legend can still die just like anyone else, and die in horrible fashion. Maybe not as easily as lower-ranked characters, but they're still quite definitely mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:27:31-08:00","id":1158615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1158608#post1158608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You really have to ask yourself if this jives with maintaining all Renown at 10 dots, because it feels like it wouldn't be very conducive to it, nor would it make the character the ne plus ultra of what they represent that legendary Rank entails. The horror, as far as Werewolf is concerned when it utilizes its particular horror genre conventions, is that the legend can still die just like anyone else, and die in horrible fashion. Maybe not as easily as lower-ranked characters, but they're still quite definitely mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course but I wonder on mood and story wise elements rather than just a bad story posibile outcome, no character lives forever, though you may indeed lose a 10 year old best friend if you kill his awesome character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T00:38:57-08:00","id":1160445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1158615#post1158615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course but I wonder on mood and story wise elements rather than just a bad story posibile outcome, no character lives forever, though you may indeed lose a 10 year old best friend if you kill his awesome character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a thing really clear to my players before starting our current campaign: Werewolf is a game about heroic battles, but there will be no plot armor for them every time they perform such an act. It's way too easy to throw yourself in some hard fight for Gaia hoping to gain renown points and fame in your sect when you think that your master won't kill you over some low level encounter, but that's not how the game should be played.<br /> If they want to survive they need to flee or mind their own businesses, because when they choose to fight I <i><u>will</u></i> kill them on a good damage roll. Heroism has only meaning when your life is at stake.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if I think that Rank 6 gifts are quite fine the way they are there has been a ritual irking me. It's the exclusive level 5 ritual know only by the Red Talon legend Sunrise-Heart, the Rite of Gaian Rebirth. By the rules (Red Talon tribebook) it requires two difficult rolls, a Moot to be called on place and permanent sacrifice of Stamina and Gnosis to create 1 acre of forest for every Stamina or two points of Gnosis erased.<br /> <br /> Now, 1 acre doesn't look much to me. Let's say that our top possible expense is 4 Stamina dots and 8 Gnosis points (You can't go stamina or gnosis zero without dying) for a total overall loss of 144 xp (of course you didn't actually pay all of them in creation, is just to calculate how much you'd need to buy them back); you get 8 square acres of forest out of this, aka 180x180 meters. It's less than city parks in the most industrialized zones of Earth, and it gets me quite confused because the manual goes to some lenghts to say &quot;Isn't this a bit overpowered? Why don't Red Talons just do this in the middle of Detroit?&quot; Well, because it would be logged down in a week and now one of your most powerful warriors can barely manage to cross the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T01:51:50-08:00","id":1160454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1160445#post1160445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made a thing really clear to my players before starting our current campaign: Werewolf is a game about heroic battles, but there will be no plot armor for them every time they perform such an act. It's way too easy to throw yourself in some hard fight for Gaia hoping to gain renown points and fame in your sect when you think that your master won't kill you over some low level encounter, but that's not how the game should be played.<br /> If they want to survive they need to flee or mind their own businesses, because when they choose to fight I <i><u>will</u></i> kill them on a good damage roll. Heroism has only meaning when your life is at stake.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the right and merciless way to run campaigns, I am with you on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1160445#post1160445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, even if I think that Rank 6 gifts are quite fine the way they are there has been a ritual irking me. It's the exclusive level 5 ritual know only by the Red Talon legend Sunrise-Heart, the Rite of Gaian Rebirth. By the rules (Red Talon tribebook) it requires two difficult rolls, a Moot to be called on place and permanent sacrifice of Stamina and Gnosis to create 1 acre of forest for every Stamina or two points of Gnosis erased.<br /> <br /> Now, 1 acre doesn't look much to me. Let's say that our top possible expense is 4 Stamina dots and 8 Gnosis points (You can't go stamina or gnosis zero without dying) for a total overall loss of 144 xp (of course you didn't actually pay all of them in creation, is just to calculate how much you'd need to buy them back); you get 8 square acres of forest out of this, aka 180x180 meters. It's less than city parks in the most industrialized zones of Earth, and it gets me quite confused because the manual goes to some lenghts to say &quot;Isn't this a bit overpowered? Why don't Red Talons just do this in the middle of Detroit?&quot; Well, because it would be logged down in a week and now one of your most powerful warriors can barely manage to cross the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>This level 5 ritual is probably too demanding, for such expediture I would make the effects of the ritual irreversible by normal means, in my opinion only another ritual, like wyrm oriented ones might be able to ruin a forest created in such a way. Chainsaws cut trees that instantly regrow and fire cannot burn the green leaves, the forest must be weakened first by mystical ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 11-19-2017, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T03:40:58-08:00","id":1160468,"title":"","content":"Well, the forest is supposed to grow and overpower ANY kind of human structure where the ritual is cast, so if you use it in NY downtown you'll have a couple of acres of lush forest developing all over sixty-stores skyscrapers.<br /> <br /> Still, it feels a bit underwhelming that the ritual scales so badly: casting it at 3 gnosis or 2 stamina lets you have a nice garden for an handful of XP and it may even be quite balanced, but at higher levels you're sacrificing a lot to gain almost nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T07:49:03-08:00","id":1160507,"title":"","content":"Well, the truth is that rank 5 Rituals tend to have permanent expediture in their prerequisites, but they also tend to be rituals that are enacted by an extremely powerful theurge, or elder, with the aid of a respectable number of experienced Garou. I would rule that the escalation should be equal to that of the caern building, replacing each caern level with 100 sqare metres (1076,42 sqare feet), so 4 gnosis or 2 stamina would heal 200 sqare metres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T12:30:16-08:00","id":1164597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6?p=1160507#post1160507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the truth is that rank 5 Rituals tend to have permanent expediture in their prerequisites, but they also tend to be rituals that are enacted by an extremely powerful theurge, or elder, with the aid of a respectable number of experienced Garou. I would rule that the escalation should be equal to that of the caern building, replacing each caern level with 100 sqare metres (1076,42 sqare feet), so 4 gnosis or 2 stamina would heal 200 sqare metres.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this sort of thing, I prefer geometric progressions. The more you pay on character Dots, the more each dot expended hurts you. Each of them makes a difference. On the other side, no matter how many square meters of forest you create at each dot spent, the larger the forest, the less each new piece means. Instead, it could escalate by doubling the result area, as an example.<br /> <br /> You could also state a greater effect for each spent dot the higher the stat in question was before the ritual. Given how XP costs escalate, that would help to compensate the sacrifice of high stats. Also, it would make greater heroes seem even more impressive for what they can do with their sacrifices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T12:49:20-07:00","id":1339676,"title":"","content":"After 2 years I still read this beautiful conversation, it makes me feel somehow nostalgic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}